> Original eight-object heap model

Retain original refs[[1],[2],[],[4],[3],[],[7],[]] with root[0]. The actual live
ids are[0,1,2], and the actual reclaimable ids are[3,4,5,6,7]. The result
vectors preserve increasing original slot order and no survivor is relocated.
The table below records each actual sweep classification and its before/after
append counts, rather than inferring a sweep sequence from the final partition.

The native plot shows actual final mark bits at their original slots. The
zero-height bars mean reclaimable in this graph model, not a measured
allocation/free-list fragment size. Size metadata is ignored because the
collector operates on object identities and unit slots.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/mark_sweep_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::mark_sweep_trace(dm::algorithms::mark_sweep_demo_graph());
    std::print("| actual original slot | actual live mark | live count before | reclaimable count before | " "live count after | reclaimable count after |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    std::vector<double> height;
    std::vector<std::string> labels;
    for (auto &s : t.sweep) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.object, s.live,
                   s.live_before, s.freed_before, s.live_after, s.freed_after);
        height.push_back(s.live);
        labels.push_back(std::format("old{}", s.object));
    }
    std::print("\nActual live count {}; actual reclaimable count {}; actual full sweep slots {}.\n",
               t.analysis.result.live.size(), t.analysis.result.freed.size(),
               t.analysis.work.scanned);
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(height, labels, "actual live mark",
                                     {37, 99, 235});
    p.x_label("original object slot").y_label("live mark1; reclaimable0");
    p.y_limits(0, 1.5).title("Original eight-object graph: actual final mark bits").save_svg("build/mark_sweep_original.svg");
}
```
