> Why an unreachable cycle remains garbage

Every marked root has a path of length zero from the roots, and every marked
field target extends such a path by one edge, proving soundness. Conversely,
induction on root-path length shows every reachable target is eventually pushed
and processed; finite mark-on-push prevents an infinite cycle. Thus the final
marks are exactly the least root-reachable closure. Scanning every old slot then
partitions all ids into disjoint live and reclaimable sets.

The original3-to4-to3 cycle has incoming references from its own members but no
path from root0. Both therefore remain unmarked and reclaimable. Basic reference
counting alone would retain such a cycle unless augmented with cycle handling.
If root3 is supplied instead, the exact same cycle becomes live: garbage is
relative to the chosen roots, not an intrinsic property of a component.

The native diagram shows original graph edges and actual final node marks. Grey
unreachable edges are part of the owned input graph and complete validation, but
were never traversed during live marking. The actual marker visits only two
live-owner fields, while complete validation checks all five original fields,
including garbage.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/mark_sweep_cycles.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::mark_sweep_trace(dm::algorithms::mark_sweep_demo_graph());
    auto &g = t.marking.graph;
    auto &r = t.analysis.result;
    std::array<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint, 8> positions{{{0, 0}, {6, 0},
                                                         {12, 0}, {0, -3},
                                                         {6, -3}, {12, -3},
                                                         {0, -6}, {6, -6}}};
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    for (int i = 0; i < g.num_objects; ++i) {
        dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;
        style.fill =
            r.marked[i] ? dm::graphics::RGB{220, 252, 231}
            : dm::graphics::RGB{241, 245, 249};
        d.node(std::to_string(i), positions[i],
               std::format("Actual old object{}\nactual live mark{}", i,
                           int(r.marked[i])), style);
    }
    std::print("| original owner | original target | actual owner live | field visited in live marking |\n| " "---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (int i = 0; i < g.num_objects; ++i)
        for (int child : g.refs[i]) {
            dm::graphics::DiagramStroke stroke;
    stroke.color =
        r.marked[i] ? dm::graphics::RGB{22, 163, 74}
        : dm::graphics::RGB{148, 163, 184};
    d.edge(std::to_string(i), std::to_string(child), {}, stroke);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, child, bool(r.marked[i]),
               bool(r.marked[i]));
        }
        std::print("\nActual complete validated fields {}; actual live-marking field visits {}.\n",
                   t.analysis.work.marking.validation.references,
                   t.analysis.work.marking.references);
        d.save_svg("build/mark_sweep_cycles.svg");
}
```
