> Root controls, actual costs and model boundaries

Complete structural validation checks the nonnegative dense object count,
exactly one reference row per object and every root/field id, including
unreachable fields. These guards occur before capture or indexing. Duplicate
roots/fields, sharing, self references and cycles are valid. Supplied size
metadata is ignored entirely by this slot-only model. The graph and its arrays
are borrowed unchanged for ordinary analysis; traces own a complete original
copy including ignored metadata.

Total validation/mark/sweep time is O(N+E+R), since all original fields must be
validated even when only a small live component is traversed. Dense marks,
pending stack and returned live/reclaimable ids require O(N) storage in addition
to input. The implementation models graph liveness and classification; it does
not destroy C++ objects, free allocator blocks, rebuild a free list, compact
payloads or implement incremental/concurrent collection. Stop-the-world
collector mechanisms are motivation rather than a claim about a running managed
heap.

The root controls below are independent collector runs on the identical original
graph, not prefix reruns for reconstructing history. They retain empty roots,
root0, root3, both components, and a duplicated root0. The actual full sweep
remains eight slots in every run, while actual live traversal changes with
reachability and duplicate roots do not duplicate discoveries.

Trace admission counts shared marking’s2*N+E+R+S base original/mark slots and
actual root/pop/live-field events, then one record per actual old-slot sweep
classification. Default cap is one million; zero disables the optional cap.
Fields, row headers, capacities, returned/runtime mark/result copies and
physical bytes are excluded. Captures contain one actual marking execution and
one actual sweep, complete or exception. A valid empty graph produces empty
vectors. No external dataset is relevant to these exact object-graph controls.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/mark_sweep_roots.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> live;
    std::vector<std::string> labels{"no roots", "root0", "root3", "roots0+3",
                                    "root0 twice"};
    std::vector<std::vector<int>> roots{{}, {0}, {3}, {0, 3}, {0, 0}};
    std::print("| prescribed root control | actual root slots examined | actual discovered live objects | " "actual live-owner fields visited | actual complete validated fields | actual sweep slots | " "actual reclaimable ids |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < roots.size(); ++i) {
        auto g = dm::algorithms::mark_sweep_demo_graph();
        g.roots = roots[i];
        auto a = dm::algorithms::mark_sweep_analyze(g);
        auto &w = a.work;
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", labels[i],
                   w.marking.roots, w.marking.marks, w.marking.references,
                   w.marking.validation.references, w.scanned,
                   a.result.freed.size());
        live.push_back(a.result.live.size());
    }
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(live, labels, "actual live count",
                                     {37, 99, 235});
    p.x_label("prescribed root set").y_label("actual live objects");
    p.y_limits(0, 8).title("Same original graph: actual root-relative liveness controls").save_svg("build/mark_sweep_roots.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| prescribed root control | actual root slots examined | actual discovered live objects | actual live-owner fields visited | actual complete validated fields | actual sweep slots | actual reclaimable ids |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| no roots | 0 | 0 | 0 | 5 | 8 | 8 |
| root0 | 1 | 3 | 2 | 5 | 8 | 5 |
| root3 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 5 | 8 | 6 |
| roots0+3 | 2 | 5 | 4 | 5 | 8 | 3 |
| root0 twice | 2 | 3 | 2 | 5 | 8 | 5 |
\image(figures/mark_sweep_roots.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual liveness under independent root choices.)
\alttext(The original unreachable cycle becomes live when rooted, duplicated roots do not duplicate discoveries, and every run still performs the complete eight-slot sweep.)

> Verification and references

Native tests exhaust all4096 three-vertex directed-graph/root-set combinations
against independent transitive closure, verify every real sweep read and
before/after partition count, and retain the original unreachable cycle/chain
and changed-root controls. Shared liveness tests inspect actual
mark/stack/root/field order, duplicate/self/cyclic references, complete invalid
unreachable fields, exact quotas, ignored sizes, ownership and a100000-object
iterative chain. Existing memory/format regression cases remain. The ten-report
batch passes 95 CTest cases, 30 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan cases, 121
compiled and executed public examples, 601/601 scoped documentation definitions
and 11 representative hovers. Independent integer, Fraction, graph, string and
NumPy references verify 82,729 records, including the complete original seeded
LSH study. Frozen comparisons preserve ordinary legacy results; malformed-input,
sentinel-collision, ownership and explicit-budget corrections are documented
above. Thirteen checkout headers and thirteen installed headers compile
independently, and an installed-header native consumer links and runs. Each
complete report program runs against the checkout library; all four native
figures are reviewed and HTML/Markdown exports preserve computed results and
image bytes. Batch receipts: `build/mepml-conversion/batch-214-223/`.

J. McCarthy(1960),
[Recursive Functions of Symbolic Expressions and Their Computation by Machine, Part I|https://www-formal.stanford.edu/jmc/recursive.html],
Communications of the ACM3(4),184–195, describes early LISP list processing and
reclamation. The report’s concrete complete-validation, mark-on-push ordering
and returned object-id vectors are explicit contracts of this native graph
model.
